Format consistency
Right now the hero card shows a weekday + full date ("Tuesday, September 29, 2026") while the timeline below drops the weekday ("October 11, 2026"). Pick one and use it everywhere — I'd drop the weekday from both. It doesn't add signal here, since "Ascending sequence" / "seconds" already tell the story. So: MMMM d, yyyy (e.g. "October 11, 2026") consistently, formatted client-side with Intl.DateTimeFormat(locale, { year:'numeric', month:'long', day:'numeric' }) so it respects the visitor's locale automatically instead of hardcoding English.

Relative vs absolute
Keep "tomorrow" as a relative label, but only for genuinely near dates (today/tomorrow/this week) — past that, relative labels ("in 14 days") get noisy next to a list of long-range milestones stretching to 2030. So: relative badge for anything within ~7 days, absolute date only beyond that. That's basically what you're already doing in the hero card; just don't extend it into the timeline list.

Vertical list — yes, but tighten it; cf claude

# tech

